{"Title":"Resolve reviving and continuing the non-emergency human services transportation task force","BillNumber":"H3302","DocketNumber":"HD4035","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"M_D2","Name":"Mindy Domb","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/M_D2","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T16:17:17.687"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"M_D2","Name":"Mindy Domb","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/M_D2","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T16:17:17.6866667"},{"Id":"SKP1","Name":"Sarah K. Peake","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SKP1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T16:17:17.8133333"},{"Id":"JPL1","Name":"Jack Patrick Lewis","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JPL1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-08T15:51:29.2"},{"Id":"JRO0","Name":"Jacob R. Oliveira","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JRO0","ResponseDate":"2023-02-17T11:01:24.5033333"},{"Id":"D_R1","Name":"David Allen Robertson","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/D_R1","ResponseDate":"2023-06-04T19:09:26.94"},{"Id":"MRS1","Name":"Margaret R. Scarsdale","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MRS1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-17T09:22:50.2466667"}],"JointSponsor":{"Id":"SKP1","Name":"Sarah K. Peake","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SKP1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T16:17:17.687"},"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3302/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Resolve","Pinslip":"By Representatives Domb of Amherst and Peake of Provincetown, a petition (accompanied by resolve, House, No. 3302) of Mindy Domb, Sarah K. Peake and others relative to reviving and continuing the task force established (under Section 134 of Chapter 24 of the Acts of 2021) on non-emergency human services transportation.  Transportation.","DocumentText":"\tResolved, That the task force established in section 134 of chapter 24 of the acts of 2021 is hereby revived and continued to December 1, 2026.\r\n\tThe task force on non-emergency human services transportation established in section 134 of chapter 24 of the acts of 2021 is hereby revived and continued; provided, however, that the task force shall file its final report and its recommendations, if any, together with drafts of legislation necessary to carry those recommendations into effect by filing the same with the clerks of the senate and house of representatives, the house and senate committees on ways and means, the joint committee on transportation, the joint committee on children, families and persons with disabilities, the secretary of health and human services and the secretary of transportation not later than December 1, 2026; and provided further, that the task force may make a draft of its final report available to the public for comment before filing it as provided herein.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Discharge to Another Committee","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J40","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J40"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}